{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/276844-apocalypse-gehenna-both-pre-and-post-setting-veil-on-verge-of-collapsing-plz-help","id":276844,"title":"Apocalypse/Gehenna both pre and post setting, Veil on verge of collapsing, plz help.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-09T17:33:35-07:00","id":276844,"title":"Apocalypse/Gehenna both pre and post setting, Veil on verge of collapsing, plz help.","content":"Okay, I have an idea for a game idea that I might want to offer to some friends of mine in the event that we ever get together again and I get to be Storyteller. The Traditions have wiped out the Black Spiral Dancers in perhaps the most epic event in the history of the WoD. First they captured ten of their Elders, 2 from each Auspice and all belonging to packs that followed Whippoorwill and each of their totem avatars are sealed in a magical fetish made from Stygian Steel. I remember how the Vortex in Malfeas is the only thing that could kill the Wyrm Talons, so my idea involved capturing a trio of Zmei, using them to open a portal to Malfeas, and then using them to get one of the two sets of Black Spiral Elders into the Vortex.<br /> <br /> The other set of Black Spiral Elders are in a conquered Hive dedicated to Whippoorwill, the spirit avatar of which is also captured and also part of the ritual. They are all carefully guarded along with nine captured Nameless, each one of which is sealed in cocoons that are based off of the webs that have captured and encapsulated the Flux. The Elders are bound and each one has had its heart forcibly traded with the Black Spiral Elders which are being brought to Malfeas. All of the Wyrm Prisoners are ringed together in a circle around a giant Stygian Steel statue of Whippoorwill, which represents the entire Tribe of Black Spiral Dancers and their Totem, since they are spiritually linked together. Eight of the Nameless have been spiritually linked and attuned to the three spirit Avatars of Whippoorwill and the 5 Black Spiral Elders. The Ninth is linked to the statue in the middle which has been linked to the prisoners and is now serving as a sort of correspondence point for the entire Tribe of Black Spiral Dancers and everyone who is a child of Whippoorwill as well as the totem itself. Normally, it would take way too much power to affect them drawing on that thin thread of correspondence, but things are about to change. At the exact moment that the first set of Elders are cast in to the Vortex the Magi use the link they created between the two groups of Black Spiral Elders to draw upon the the Wyld power possessed by the Vortex in Malfeas into the 5 Black Spiral Elders, and through them to the rest of the group they have captured including the Nameless who are all linked to the group. The prison cocoons of the Nameless are altered so that they are each at that moment pushed into a choice, submit to being named or tear off the names of the beings that they have been linked and attuned to in order to assure that they can do it without a problem. The first Eight Nameless draws upon the power that is flowing through the matrix that has been built around them to rip off the names of the Avatars and the Elders, but the ninth, channeling the the magics of the Magi, the power of the Vortex in Malfeas, and the wave of momentum that is at that moment emanating all around it thanks to the names which have already been ripped off, a momentum that was already foreseen and was prepared for by the mages to be used by the ninth nameless, and rips off the name of Whippoorwill and its entire Tribe, and every Nephandi or rogue Fera that followed it.<br /> <br /> Now, all through the world and the Umbra it is the equivalent of nukes going off and destroying the physical and spiritual landscape. Malfeas didn't react well to an Incarna suddenly having its name destroyed and being turned into a mega nuke, so while some of the rulers are still around they are probably keeping their heads down while they figure out what just happened. The entirety of Earth is in hysterics as rogue nukes that left no radiation behind went off and no one is taking responsibility for what just happened. Everything seems to be falling apart, even in the wake of a defeated Wyrm. The Traditions are probably decimated, but lets assume they foresaw the world ending immediately unless they performed this act to buy the world some more time to get ready before doomsday. What happens now? This is where I want the story to begin, but I would like some input as to what the wreckage of the world and the Umbra should look like, both in the natural and supernatural world, before I pitch this idea to anyone.<br /> <br /> EDIT: One idea that I have is that the Technocracy would love to begin a new Pogrom on what mages are left, but that they can't because they suddenly have their hands full, and that the explosions from the Umbra is causing the equivalent of a new Avatar Storm that is giving them all sorts of reasons to stay busy and out of the Traditions hair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 10-09-2014, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T17:48:28-07:00","id":276861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/276844-apocalypse-gehenna-both-pre-and-post-setting-veil-on-verge-of-collapsing-plz-help#post276844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything seems to be falling apart, even in the wake of a defeated Wyrm</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have missed something. Where, in all of that, was the Wyrm defeated ?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T18:02:17-07:00","id":276874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/276844-apocalypse-gehenna-both-pre-and-post-setting-veil-on-verge-of-collapsing-plz-help?p=276861#post276861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I must have missed something. Where, in all of that, was the Wyrm defeated ?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, eff me. I guess its too late to correct that. Not at all defeated, but maybe some of his bigger hitters are a little stunned or even dead depending on where they were when the blasts went off. Especially if they were anywhere near Whippoorwill when he detonated. Also, his plans to bring about the Apocalypse might need to go back to the drawing board since some of his favorite and most legendary shock troops have been reduced to subatomic particals and some of the big fetishes and artifacts that he was planning to unleash for the end game have been destroyed. For practical purposes, the Wyrm simply has a few job openings now, and Malfeas might be slightly easier to enter and exit of for a couple of months or even years. Also, the Apocalypse might have been pushed back a generation or two as a number of banes are called home to add some extra security to Malfeas and the Wyrm needs time to rebuild everything that was lost, which was just about everything that was standing anywhere near a BSD at the time. Disregard what you just quoted me as saying, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 10-09-2014, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}